{number: 29}
{title: Angels We Have Heard on High}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Angels we have [G] heard on [C] high,
Sweetly singing [G] o'er the [C] plains,
And the mountains [G] in re-[C] ply
Echoing their [G] joyous [C] strains.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] Glo-[Am]-[Dm]-[G7]-[C]-[F]-[G] ria, [C] in ex-[G] celsis [C] De-[G] o!
[C] Glo-[Am]-[Dm]-[G7]-[C]-[F]-[G] ria, [C] in ex-[G] celsis [C] De-[G7]-[C] o!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Shepherds, why this [G] jubi-[C] lee?
Why your joyous [G] strains pro-[C] long?
Say what may the [G] tidings [C] be,
Which inspire your [G] heav'nly [C] song?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Come to Bethlehem, [G] and [C] see
Him whose birth the [G] angels [C] sing;
Come, adore on [G] bended [C] knee
Christ the Lord, the [G] newborn [C] King.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C] See within a [G] manger [C] laid
Jesus, Lord of [G] heav'n and [C] earth!
Mary, Joseph, [G] lend your [C] aid,
With us sing our [G] Savior's [C] birth.
{end_of_verse}
